    "_comment": "RigCheck by ShackDesk — how a radio names itself, mapped to its Hamlib model number. Kenwood, Elecraft, and Yaesu CAT rigs answer 'ID;' with 'IDnnn;'. Icom rigs answer a CI-V read-ID with their own CI-V address (two hex digits); Reply holds that address. Where several rigs share one reply (Elecraft K3 / KX3 / KX2 all answer ID017;), the first entry is the default and the others are listed so a selected preset can override. Model numbers follow Hamlib's riglist.h: thousands = backend (1 Yaesu, 2 Kenwood/Elecraft, 3 Icom). Validate at jsonlint.com; corrections and additions welcome — see CONTRIBUTING.md."
  },

